1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A cyclic arbitrage normally reconciles three
inconsistent pools by executing three swaps.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Even when profit is reinjected, the EVM still
pays to replay every leg.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,000
ARBFOLD asks whether cooperating v4 pools can
settle the equivalent state directly.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:35,000
At canonical 100k, the reference executes two rounds:
six arbitrage swaps and two reinjections.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:45,000
One fold() call applies two direct rounds. At 100k:
544,219 gas versus 375,171, or 31.06% less.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The Swap Lab uses three explicitly valueless test tokens:
ARFX, ARFY and ARFZ.

7
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:03,000
It reads the deployed quote without a signature and
shows the complete three-pool cycle.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Wallet preparation mints only a deficit and approves
only the selected amount.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The final action sends one real swap plus fold to the
public v0.1 deployment.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:28,000
The user output and fixed external-recipient reward
are exactly equal in both controlled paths.

11
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The six final reserves are compared losslessly and
are equivalent within the measured one-wei tolerance.

12
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
At 25k: 409,402 gas versus 329,777,
or 19.45% less.

13
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The 1k through 4k execute zero fold rounds and
remain more expensive.

14
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
From 5k through 200k, 196 of 196 actionable
workloads were cheaper in the tested canonical path.

15
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,000
That is path-specific experimental evidence,
not a universal savings claim.

16
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:15,000
The controlled benchmark alone compares identical
starting states and supplies the gas result.

17
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:24,000
The public Unichain Sepolia receipt proves execution
of the public v0.1 deployment.

18
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,000
It contains one SwapAndFold, two FoldRound events and
FoldCompleted with zero residual.

19
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The historical v0 research deployment remains archived
and is not the primary submission deployment.

20
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:50,000
The hook computes user output first, then invokes the
fixed coordinator in the same PoolManager unlock.

21
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
The coordinator transfers backed ERC-6909 claims and
checks conservation and non-decreasing invariants.

22
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:09,000
The current suite contains 82 Solidity tests in both
default and 10,000-run release profiles.

23
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:17,000
It covers all six paths, stateful invariants,
negative cases and exact PoolManager backing.

24
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:25,000
The proof command also checks the lossless benchmark,
source manifest and public deployment facts.

25
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:34,000
We preregistered a stronger claim: ten percent more
LP net value. It failed.

26
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:43,000
The measured improvement was only 0.000287 percent
in that frozen environment.

27
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Historical results remain immutable. What survived is
an execution advantage in tested actionable workloads.

28
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Steady-state telemetry gas is not claimed because it
has not been measured across real transactions.

29
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:07,000
ARBFOLD is research-grade, not production-audited and
does not claim universal MEV protection.

30
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Don’t replay every leg.
Settle the equivalent state.
